  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_19457",
  "verbalization": "Decitabine is associated with Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome through a mechanism involving its use in treating Acute Myeloid Leukemia and related conditions. The evidence suggests that Decitabine, through its indication for Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia and Acute Myeloid Leukemia with specific chromosomal abnormalities, may contribute to the development of Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome. This is supported by the indirect pathway through Ivosidenib, which is indicated for Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome, suggesting a potential role of Decitabine in the pathogenesis of this condition. The overlapping indications and the shared therapeutic outcomes imply a possible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
